 - Unsaved form input is instance state. The manifest editor's edits live in its instance's ui record through `state/forms/manifest-draft.ts`. An entry form's typed values live in a record of their own beside the instance's, `<id>#forms`, through `state/forms/form-drafts.svelte.ts`, keyed by the collection and the entry's id or null for adding; most host views write their own record whole from a parse of their own keys, which is why a form's drafts are not inside it. Which add and edit forms are open is instance state too (`state/forms/open-forms.ts`, read into the Collection, Pillars, Domains, Venues and Data states), so a form comes back open with what was typed into it; the Files view keeps its open form, the bookmark it edits, the line typed into its root or workspace form and a count of the presses that opened or closed a form as `form`, `editing`, `typed` and `opening` of `FilesView` (`state/sources/fs.ts`), and the refusal and outcome lines that answered its last press as `note` and `said`, written into the instance the request went from. A press that closes or moves the bookmark form forgets its draft through `toggleAdd` or `toggleEdit` under the `bookmarks` collection key, and so does the edited bookmark leaving the loaded list, read by `editedGone` through the fs store's `closeGoneForms` on every bookmarks answer that came back, over every file browser the layout holds (`BookmarkForms`, wired in `state/client/context.ts`), so a browser in a tab never shown, or on a page drawing none, is closed with the rest; a form a save of its own is out from is left until that answer lands (`beginFormSave`, `endFormSave`), and a bookmark form whose own save writes the bookmark under a new id is carried onto it, draft and all (`onrenamed`, `moveFormDraft`), so nothing is gone to close. A write takes the instance id and the forms before its request goes and closes a form on its answer only when that instance still holds that opening as the request left it (`formSettled`), since the answer may land after the tab closed or the form was reopened; the bookmark form takes both when it mounts, once per instance and opening (`views/sources/files/sections/BookmarkForm.svelte`). A Files instance whose root or workspace line holds text other than spaces registers with `registerUnsaved` (`filesLineTyped`, wired in `state/client/context.ts` by the instance's view). Each tab view a pane mounts puts the reader of its instance into a component context (`state/client/instance-context.ts`), so the form finds its instance without a prop through its callers, and a form outside a pane keeps its values in a local target and registers nothing. Whether a draft is unsaved is decided against the entry as the snapshot holds it now, through the save's own rule in `state/forms/form-values.ts`; a draft whose entry the snapshot's collection no longer holds is never counted and is dropped at the instance's next draft write, and an add form or an entry outside the snapshot's collections is compared with what its controls opened holding. Both stores register with `registerUnsaved` beside `sourceDirty`, so a tab holding either asks before it closes. Cancel, a form's close by the view's Add or Edit control, a delete, Revert and a save forget the draft, an edit's save keeping what was typed after it went, and an add's save forgetting its draft and closing the form only while the draft is still what the save sent (`takeFormDraft`), a form left open going on to write the entry it made, kept beside the draft under `<id>#added`, until its identity field is typed away from that entry. A tab's close, a pane's close and a page's close forget the state and the form drafts of every instance they take away; a page one of the closed page's leaves shows is not closed with it, and its instances keep theirs.
-- Files and Repositories read as an explorer and a source control view. Rows are drawn by `ui/tree/TreeItem.svelte`. A row is one fixed-height line holding an indent guide per level (shown while its tree is hovered or holds the focus), an expand arrow on a row that opens, a glyph or, given `file`, the file's Seti icon (`ui/display/FileIcon.svelte`), name, muted detail, the row's controls (`ui/tree/TreeActions.svelte`, transparent until the row is hovered or holds the focus, except a section head given `showActions`, which the Notes and Bookmarks heads are, drawn at full strength always; and always drawn on a screen whose pointer does not hover; a view sets `--action-pad` to draw the padding round the 16 px icon closer, as the Repositories view does with 1 px; the box is 20 px from the compact control's `min-width` and `height` of `--header-action`, with no border), and a count or mark, which sit `--tree-end-inset` from the row's edge (6 px; the Repositories view sets 12 px, a section head keeps 6); the count of a section head or a change group is a badge (`badge`, with `countTitle` for its hover words). A heading row is uppercase at weight 700. A row may also be `strong` (weight 600, the head commit), `struck`, given a `nameStyle`, `trailing` (its mark before its controls, for a graph row's pills), `yielding` (its controls give way before the name) or the `link` tone (centred words in the link colour). The name part (the `.main` rule of `ui/tree/TreeItem.svelte`, `flex: 1 1 auto`) takes the row's free width with the detail inside it, so the row's controls, count and status letter sit at the pane's right edge and the letters of a list read down one column; the row spans the pane for its hover and its selection, and a press anywhere on the name part opens it as a press on the name does. The detail, the count and the mark are drawn at the small size (`--fs-sm`), and a view that wants a detail part larger sizes it from `--tree-font` in its own rule, as the change row's folder and status letter and the graph row's author do (90% of the row's size). Its height, indent and two type sizes are `--tree-row`, `--tree-indent`, `--tree-font` and `--tree-heading-font` of `themes/tokens.css` (22, 8, 13 and 11 px; `--tree-badge-size` and `--tree-badge-font` size a badge, 18 and 11 px, `--graph-lane` one lane of the graph, 11 px, and `--icon-box` the 16 px box of a row's icon, status letter and icon control; a badge and a graph pill draw their figures in the interface font with tabular figures), each multiplied by the text scale where the row is drawn, so an ancestor may set either. Selected is the reader's cursor, the accent tint under `--on-accent-bg`; current is what is in force, a bold name with a check. A row's tooltip opens on pointer hover only, and its words describe the row, the element that takes the focus in a tree. Rows sit in `ui/tree/TreeView.svelte`, a `tree` that is one stop of the focus order, run by zag's tree-view machine (`@zag-js/tree-view` through `@zag-js/svelte`) over the collection `ui/tree/tree-keys.ts` builds from the caller's rows: Up and Down step a row, Home and End go to the ends, Right opens a closed row and steps into an open one, Left closes an open row and steps out to its parent, a letter moves to the next row whose label starts with it (type-ahead), a letter with Cmd or Ctrl held is left to the browser, and a row marked `fixed` is stepped through and never opened or closed. Whether a row is open and which row is selected stay the caller's. Each row is a `treeitem` with its level that takes the focus, and Enter presses it. Its controls take tabindex 0 only while the focus is inside the row, so Tab from a row reaches them and Tab from outside does not. The three lists with no cap on their rows (the Files tree's rows, the Repositories view's changed files and the commit graph's loaded commits) draw only the rows in view through `ui/tree/list/VirtualRows.svelte` (`@tanstack/virtual-core`), against the pane body that scrolls, with spacers holding the height of the rows not drawn and the row height read from `--tree-row` as drawn. The row holding the tree's stop, the row the focus is in and the graph's open commit stay drawn wherever the list is scrolled, so Tab always reaches the tree, a scroll never takes the focus out of it and the open commit's files are read once. A key moving to a row not drawn scrolls it in first, and a type-ahead reads the names of rows not drawn. Until a list has found its scroll box it draws its first ten rows and holds the rest at `--tree-row`. Every other tree list is drawn whole. Sections are `ui/tree/TreeSection.svelte`. The Files view's tree starts with the workspace header (`views/sources/files/header/WorkspaceHeader.svelte`), a 22 px pane header that is the first row of the same `TreeView` (`withHeader` in `state/sources/explorer/rows/tree-rows.ts`, so the arrow keys walk from it into the roots) with four actions, New File, New Folder, Refresh Explorer and Collapse Folders in Explorer, and a `...` menu whose items Add Folder to Workspace, Switch Workspace, Save Workspace As and Open Folder, and the checked Show Hidden Files, Show Ignored Files and File Nesting, are the only place the workspace is changed from the page; Switch Workspace, Save Workspace As and Open Folder open the palette with `:workspace`, `:workspace-save` and `:folder` typed (`ui.requestPalette`), where `shell/keys/Palette.svelte` runs them. Every root is a top-level folder row under the header. A tab rooted at a folder (`top` in its instance state, set by `showFolderInFiles`) or following a session draws no header, and a rooted one has the `..` row above its top. The view's toolbar holds the follow toggle and the pin, and its bar the filter box with the Fuzzy Match toggle, so all exist in every state. Add Folder to Workspace runs `POST /api/folders/pick` (`server/files/fs/picker.ts`, which opens the macOS folder panel through one injectable runner and lists and serves nothing), and the folders it returns become roots through the `roots` write: in the default workspace the entries of `sources.yml`'s `roots:` (the write kind `roots` of `server/edit/writes.ts`, built on `server/edit/list-edit.ts`, recorded in the change log with its undo), in a named workspace `workspaces.json`. File nesting is the pattern map of `config/catalogs/file-nesting.yml` (`data/helpers/files/nesting.ts`, the one rule the page and the server's findings share). Its instance keeps `expanded`, `selected: { root, path }`, `selection` and `anchor` (the rows selected with the cursor row), `filter`, `fuzzy`, `collapsed` and `opened` (the sections closed and the ones opened, since Open Editors, Outline and Timeline start closed), `timelinePinned` (the file the Timeline is held on, or null), `timelineGit` and `timelineLocal` (the two lists the Timeline shows, both true by default), `top`, `outside`, `hidden`, `ignored` and `nesting` (all three false by default; the first two are sent as `hidden=1` and `ignored=1` on each listing, each pair of them a listing of its own in the fs store, and a flip re-reads every folder held under the pair it names through `relist`), and the three keys of an ask to show a path: `reveal` (`{ root, path, asked, settled }`, with `open: true` for a folder shown open and `timeline: true` for Open Timeline, which opens the Timeline section and scrolls to it in place of the row), `revealed` (the last outcome not found as asked) and `revealing` (the count of asks). A project card draws the same tree (`views/shared/explorer/ProjectTree.svelte` over `rooted-tree.svelte.ts`) rooted at the project's folder, as the head of the tree with the `folderView` rule of `state/sources/explorer/view/tab-roots.ts` that follow mode uses, in a box of its own bounded height that is the scroll box its rows are windowed against (`data-scroll`). A card keeps a record of the same shape as the tab's instance state under `<tab instance id>#files:<project id>`, the project id percent-encoded (`cardTreeKey` in `state/sources/explorer/view/card-tree.ts`), written when the card is drawn (the project folder open), cleared with the tab by a prefix clear in `state/client/context.ts`'s forget, and restated by `followTabs` when a rename or a move changes a path it holds; the finder box above the tree keeps its text in that record's `filter`, and the project's file listing (`files(id)`) is asked for only while that text is not empty. The filter walks every listing already read under the tab's toggles (`heldEntries` asks the server for nothing) and draws a match open under its folders, holding those folders `fixed` and writing nothing to `expanded`, so clearing it restores the tree. A row star bookmarks under the file's name, or under its path under the root when the name is already a label. Removing a root asks first. The Repositories list offers every root of the `git` channel, labelled by last folder or by the last two where two share it (`pickerRoots`, `repositoryLabels`, `shownRoot`), and the view keeps `root`, `collapsed` (the closed sections, groups and folders; a folder's id is `dir:<root>:<group>:<path>`), the graph's open commit, `commit`, the `mode` of the changes and the `reveal` request of a row's Branch control. An empty staged group is not drawn, and a status letter's colour (`statusStyle`) and the line counts (`shared/changes/ChangeCounts.svelte`) are shared with the session views' Changes panel.
