pActions.svelte`, handed up through `ui/tabs/tab-actions.svelte.ts`), and the save outcome stays as a line under the editor. The Files tree draws no breadcrumb. A Terminal tab is titled by `terminalTabTitle` of `state/sessions/terminal/terminal-lists.ts` (the reader's title, else the agent's word, else the project command's name, else the process tmux reports, else the word for a shell), which only the tab uses; the Sessions view's rows and the Processes view keep `terminalLabel` (title, else name), and a terminal's viewport line, and whether it sat at the end, are kept per terminal when its grid goes (`state/sessions/terminal/viewport.ts`), so Float and Return to Page leave the scrollback where it was. A dialog (`ui/frame/Modal.svelte`) and the Memories picture overlay are drawn into the document body through `portal` of `ui/shown.ts`, outside the area that holds the floats, so they stand over a float; a dialog takes the focus once its bindings are set (`focusOnOpen` of `ui/frame/quiet-focus.ts`), and the Memories overlay gives it back through `focusQuietly`. The page cancels the browser's own context menu everywhere an oculus menu does not open (`shouldCancel` of `shell/context-guard.ts`, one document `contextmenu` listener in `routes/+page.svelte`), and leaves it inside a text input, a textarea, a contenteditable element, the code editor and the terminal grid.
