+    // file, not per tab, so an answer that lands after the tab closed or was pointed at another
+    // file draws nothing and throws nothing. A file that cannot be read says so with the source
+    // tab's words, a file longer than the read window says so above its first part with the source
+    // tab's words, and a saved state naming no file says none was chosen.
+    //
+    // The tab draws no row of controls and hands none to the pane's strip: the bookmark and Open in
+    // Program items are in the tab's right-click menu (shell/panes/strip/tab-menu.ts). The
+    // rendering is shared/prose/RenderedMarkdown.svelte, which the source tab's rendered half draws
+    // too; here its scroll box is where the keyboard goes when a double click keeps the tab
+    // (PaneBody.svelte). The headings it draws are said to the Outline, and a press on an Outline
+    // row scrolls the tab to that heading (shared/prose/rendered-headings.svelte.ts).
